WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.234
-Why is everyone bringing me
gifts today?

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.067
-It's Giving Tuesday.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.267
-It is giving, yes.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:07.000
-So I thought I would give you
some of these.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.968
They've only just come out.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.100
Hopefully they fit you.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.067
They're Avatar sneakers.
They're skate shoes.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:14.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:15.968
-No way.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.033
-Come on, that's what
I'm talking about, bud.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.267
That's a friend.
-You're welcome.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.534
-That's a friend right there.

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.334
Thank you very much for these.
I appreciate them.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.534
-I think they glow
in the dark too.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.300
They light up like
bioluminescence.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.100
-Come on. Dude, is that right?

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.067
-So when you skate in the dark,
as you do.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.434
-Yeah, I do skate. I do skate
in the dark. It'll glow?

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.667
-Yeah.
-Thanks for coming back.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.634
But I haven't seen you
in so long.

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:39.667
-It's been a while.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.634
-You're a great friend
of our show.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.968
Thank you for coming back
because when we first started in

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.934
"Late Night,"
you came on back in 2010.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.067
-A lot's changed. Yeah.
-You have three kids now.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.367
-Yeah.
-Congratulations.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.667
-And same to you.
-Yeah, I have two kids.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.868
How old are the kids?

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.934
-7, 6, and 2 1/2.
-Is that right?

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:00.567
-So it's a zoo.
-It is a zoo, huh?

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:04.133
-Yeah, and they're born
in America.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:07.067
I love America. One was born
in -- two were born in L.A.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.667
[ Cheers ]
Yep, and one was born

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.300
in New York
because I wanted that rivalry.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.100
-Oh that's smart.
Yeah, East Coast, West Coast.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.167
That's so smart, yeah.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:15.801
-One's Biggie,
one's Tupac for sure.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.667
-Do they have accents?
Australian accents?

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.167
-No, they've got
American accents.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.367
-They do?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.100
And they make fun of my accent
all the time.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.567
[ Laughter ]
Like, "G'day, Dad. How are ya?"

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.100
It's actually a really bad
accent that they do.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.501
-That's fun. That's great.
-Well, no, it's embarrassing.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.567
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, of course.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:36.868
But that's what kids do.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:39.601
You look great, by the way.
You look like a stud.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:41.667
You brought a photo of you
not too long ago.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.167
Here's you -- This is me with a
beard. Here is you with a beard.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:48.100
Boi-oi-oing!

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.601
-Yeah, that was my COVID beard.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:53.868
Took about nine months,
and then I kind of went,

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:56.067
"Well, I want to get a job
where I could actually

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:59.801
put that in a film"
'cause you have to.

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.701
-I mean, you put a lot of work
into growing the beard.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.133
-I did a Western.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:07.334
And I was terrible in it, but
the beard will win an Oscar.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.100
[ Laughter ]
-Congratulations.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.267
An early congratulations on
the beard winning an Oscar.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.567
You got to come back
when that comes out.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:18.267
Let's talk about "Avatar,"

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:22.200
which is I think oddly
what we did years ago.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.133
-Yeah, yeah.
-We talked about "Avatar."

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.634
And then they were like, "Yeah,
we're going to make sequels.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.000
We're going to make three.
We're going to make four."

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.300
This is --
-I saw it last night.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.901
It literally got locked off
on Saturday.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:35.000
A couple of days ago,
and then we saw it yesterday.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.267
-What did you think?

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:39.934
-It's that, man.
-Really?

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:42.968
-It's the first one,
it blows it away.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.267
I get quite emotional
talking about it

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:48.534
'cause what Jim's done,
he's made it about a family.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.968
And it's powerful.

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:52.367
It's powerful.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:55.534
Not only is it visually stunning
and you're seeing a part of

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.901
Pandora that you've never seen
before, all under water,

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.968
but it's about what you do
to protect your family.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.200
And I think after COVID,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.968
I think everybody needs
that kind of message.

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:06.200
And it's about what you would do
for those that you love.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.701
-Wow.
-Yeah, it's amazing.

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:10.234
-It's amazing how you can do
this with the technology.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.033
I remember seeing the first
"Avatar" and going like,

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.200
"Oh, I'll be into this.
This is a 3-D movie."

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.634
And I go, "It'll be a cartoon
or whatever it is."

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.734
-Well, this one, we literally --
we do scenes --

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.968
I did a scene with a kid;
he plays my son.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.601
And it's about -- you know,
the whole way through,

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.901
the fathers and sons
are disconnected.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.167
And just like teenage boys,
they're struggling to find

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.167
their place in the world.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:32.534
And we're doing the scene and I
realize I'm 30 feet under water.

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:34.300
And that's how we do
these scenes.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:38.434
We put emotional scenes
in a big tank with no scuba.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.734
We all learned how to free dive,
this great technique.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:42.767
-Yeah, we had Sigourney Weaver
on and she said she learned --

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.767
-She's part fish.
It's incredible.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.501
[ Laughter ]
-Is she really?

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.801
-She's got gills.
But no, it's amazing.

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:52.000
-How long can you hold
your breath underwater?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.834
-Well, Kate Winslet
did seven minutes.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:56.334
Sigourney did about six.
I did easy 15 seconds.

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:01.167
-So your scenes are very quick.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.734
-No, but the thing was,
when you're under that deep,

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:05.667
you have to forget that
you're under the water.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.467
And as I said, the scene between
me and this boy,

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.467
he just reached out
and squeezed my hand

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:12.367
and brought me
back into the scene.

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.934
And you forget
how submerged you are.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.868
These scenes are hard enough
to do on dry land

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:19.300
and we're just crazy enough
to put them underwater.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:23.100
-Yeah, just acting in general.
I go, "Oh, that's amazing."

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.033
But then, yeah,
like you're saying --

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.000
-Deep dive, yeah.
-Five minutes and you go like,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.000
when they say "cut,"
you still have to go --

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.968
-You can hear Jim
under the water too.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.901
So he directs you through
these sound systems in the tank.

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.767
And that's this voice
in your head going --

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.501
-How long does it take you
to get out of the water?

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.300
-I'm 46.
It took me a long time.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.734
-Don't you go like,
"Hey, when you say cut,

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.000
I got another 10 seconds
before I get oxygen"?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.601
-They would bring the scuba over
on cut and I wouldn't come up.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.267
It was easier for me
to stay down there

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:53.334
because it was a long way up, so
I would spend hours down there.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.801
And the rest of the camera team
is down there with you,

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.801
and safety coordinators.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:05:01.033
But I would do my breathe-ups
under the water.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.300
It was quite calm. Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.200
You just really lived --
-You come out like a prune.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.701
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:10.334
I know this is the second one,
"The Way of Water,"

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:13.634
and there's rumors that
there's five in the works.

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.767
How many have you filmed?
Can you say?

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:18.934
-We've filmed about
80%, 90% of three.

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:21.300
I think we're still
owing some scenes.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.267
And in four, we did a few scenes
because the kids were aging out.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.767
So we have to go --

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:28.234
-Do it before they get older.
-Before they get a bit older.

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.367
And then yeah,
there's five in the saga

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.133
if we're lucky enough to get it.

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:35.100
We're not arrogant enough to
assume it's going to connect.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.300
We really hope so because we
love the movie

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.567
and hope other people do too.

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.701
-Congratulations on this
and the first one.

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:43.801
And thank you for coming back.
Thank you for my gift.

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:45.501
-You're welcome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:48.267
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Sam Worthington in

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:51.367
"Avatar: The Way of Water."
Take a look this.

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:54.133
-If the people harbor us,
they will die.

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:57.067
Do you understand?

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:03.167
Look, I got nothing.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:04.734
I got no plan.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.534
But I can protect this family.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.000
That I can do.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.167
But I know one thing.

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:31.934
Wherever we go,
this family is our fortress.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:35.000
-Yeah, that's Sam Worthington,
everybody!

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.467
"Avatar: The Way of Water" is in
theaters and IMAX December 16th.

